---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<Layout title="About & Transparency · gh-breakout">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div>
        <h1>About gh-breakout</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          An open, zero-cost, verifiable machine learning system predicting early breakout GitHub repositories.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>What We Do</h2>
        <p>
          Every day, thousands of new open-source repositories are pushed to GitHub. A tiny fraction (&lt; 0.5%) will experience explosive adoption and gain hundreds or thousands of stars over the subsequent month.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>gh-breakout</strong> analyzes the public GitHub event stream (stars, forks, commits, issue discussions, contributor networks, and co-starrers) using machine learning to identify breakout candidates before they appear on GitHub Trending or social media.
        </p>
        <p>
          Crucially, we publish every prediction to an immutable public ledger and hold our models accountable to an honest, public track record with zero revisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Zero-Cost Architecture ($0 / month)</h2>
        <p>
          The entire project is engineered to operate on $0 infrastructure without requiring a credit card anywhere:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
          <li><strong>Compute:</strong> GitHub Actions standard Linux runners for daily ingestion, feature engineering, and model training.</li>
          <li><strong>Storage:</strong> Parquet data lake hosted publicly on <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Yasshh814/gh-breakout-events" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hugging Face Datasets</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Query Engine:</strong> Embedded DuckDB and dbt for lightning-fast local SQL transformations.</li>
          <li><strong>Website:</strong> Static Astro output hosted on GitHub Pages with client-side DuckDB-WASM for in-browser SQL exploration.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Data Sources and Attributions -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2>Data Sources & Credits</h2>
      <p>
        This project is made possible thanks to generous public data initiatives across the open-source ecosystem:
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Source</th>
              <th>Provider / Author</th>
              <th>Usage</th>
              <th>License / Terms</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>GH Archive</strong></td>
              <td>Ilya Grigorik (<a href="https://www.gharchive.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gharchive.org</a>)</td>
              <td>Hourly GitHub public event archives (2015–present)</td>
              <td>Public Domain / Creative Commons</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>GitHub API</strong></td>
              <td>GitHub, Inc.</td>
              <td>Metadata, language classification, and owner types via GraphQL</td>
              <td>Standard API terms</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Hacker News Search API</strong></td>
              <td>Algolia &amp; Y Combinator</td>
              <td>Historical and real-time stories mentioning github.com</td>
              <td>Public Algolia HN API</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>GitHub Trending Archives</strong></td>
              <td>Ronan Takizawa, Anton Komarev, Lars Bijl</td>
              <td>Wayback-archived daily trending repository snapshots (2013–2026)</td>
              <td>MIT License</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Hugging Face Hub</strong></td>
              <td>Hugging Face</td>
              <td>Public dataset and model hosting for the Parquet lake</td>
              <td>Free Community Tier</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Repository Opt-Out Policy -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
      <h2>Repository Opt-Out Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We respect developer privacy and maintainer preferences. If you are the owner or lead maintainer of a repository and do not wish for it to be featured on our public leaderboard or repo detail pages:
      </p>
      <ol style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Open an issue on our GitHub repository with the title <code>Opt-out request: owner/repo</code>.</li>
        <li>Your repository will be added to <code>config/hidden_repos.yaml</code>.</li>
        <li>On the next daily publication run, your repository will be immediately excluded from the public leaderboard, detail pages, and static exports.</li>
      </ol>
      <a href="https://github.com/Yash-814800/GH-Breakout/issues/new?title=Opt-out+request" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-github">
        Open an Opt-Out Issue →
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Star Pattern Review Policy (Phase 11) -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--border-color);">
      <h2>Star Pattern Audit &amp; Review Policy</h2>
      <p>
        The leaderboard features a neutral <em>"Unusual star pattern"</em> indicator based on statistical metrics (such as tight hourly bursts, accounts younger than 30 days, or lockstep co-starring networks).
        This signal is designed to protect leaderboard integrity and is <strong>not an accusation</strong> of intentional manipulation — genuine organic events (such as mentions in popular newsletters or community forums) can occasionally produce similar velocity patterns.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your repository has been flagged and you believe the traffic was legitimate organic growth:
      </p>
      <ol style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <li>Review the signal breakdown on your repository's detail page.</li>
        <li>Open an issue using our <a href="https://github.com/Yash-814800/GH-Breakout/issues/new?template=review-request.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review Request Issue Template</a>.</li>
        <li>Include any public links (e.g. viral post, launch announcement, or conference demo) explaining the sudden inflow of stars.</li>
        <li>Our team audits the stargazer network and applies a review annotation or exception where appropriate.</li>
      </ol>
      <a href="https://github.com/Yash-814800/GH-Breakout/issues/new?template=review-request.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-github">
        Request Star Pattern Review →
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Legal Disclaimer -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Legal Notice</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 0;">
        <strong>gh-breakout</strong> is an independent open-source research project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or associated in any way with GitHub, Inc., Microsoft Corporation, or any of their affiliates. "GitHub" and the GitHub Octocat logo are registered trademarks of GitHub, Inc. All repository names, descriptions, and code metrics remain the property of their respective authors under their declared open-source licenses.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
